press the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492009 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "440dba75-f7b2-58cf-a6ca-48d08f37cab9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492009 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy solving the second equation for ${x}_{2}$ and substituting it into the first equation, we obtain the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})^{2}+4({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})(-{y}_{2})-2(-{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}-4{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+4{y}_{2}^{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}-6{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492048 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492048 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94173" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492048 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492048 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492048 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b33e8694-c024-57a8-931b-47647a74ca8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492048 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy solving the first equation for ${x}_{2}$ and substituting it into the first equation, we obtain the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})^{2}+(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2}){y}_{1}+2{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =8{y}_{1}^{2}-8{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =12{y}_{1}^{2}-9{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492057 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492057 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94100" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492057 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492057 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ in terms of the components of $y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492057 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ccf607c0-6726-51f8-81e9-1147263496f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492057 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\ngives the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})^{2}+(3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})(-{y}_{2})-(-{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & =18{y}_{1}^{2}+24{y}_{2}{y}_{1}+8{y}_{2}^{2}-3{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =18{y}_{1}^{2}+21{y}_{2}{y}_{1}+5{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
